  "worked_solution": "To find the $y$-intercepts of the paraboloid, we substitute $x=0$ and $z=0$ in the equation of the paraboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-2)^{2}-2(y-4)^{2} & =0+4 \\\\ 4-2(y-4)^{2} & =4 \\\\ 2(y-4)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y-4 & =0 \\\\ y & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercept with the $y$-axis is $(0,4,0).$",
